.TH "GF-ANNOTATIONS-POST-GRAPHITE-ANNOTATION" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-annotations-post-graphite-annotation - Creates annotation in graphite format


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf annotations post-graphite-annotation [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates annotation in graphite format

.PP
Creates an annotation by using Graphite-compatible event format. The \fBwhen\fR and \fBdata\fR fields are optional. If \fBwhen\fR is not specified then the current time will be used as annotation’s timestamp. The \fBtags\fR field can also be in prior to Graphite \fB0.10.0\fR format (string with multiple tags being separated by a space).

.PP
Body schema (PostGraphiteAnnotationsCmd):
{
  "data": string,
  "tags": any,
  "what": string,
  "when": number
}


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	The path to the body json file or json string. For example, --body=/path/to/body.json or --body='{"foo": "bar"}'

.PP
\fB--describe-body-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the request body and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for post-graphite-annotation


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-annotations(1)\fP
